WEBVTT

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:22.710
Lorea, could you decrease the display space
used for the cooling hats?

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:25.040
Right, got it.

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:28.880
Do you think the sales have slowed down
due to that matter with Gree Dilly

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:32.750
causing so many frostfang bat
fangs to enter the market?

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:36.130
Hmm, it's not just that.

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:39.460
The fact that it's now autumn rather than
summer may be having the bigger impact.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:40.830
I see.

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:43.880
It makes sense that the cooling hats
would be a seasonal item.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:49.420
And I'm sure it's tough in a lot of ways being a
creditor for those novice alchemists, right?

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:50.580
Just a bit.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:55.040
I'm at the point where I'd really like
to turn a profit soon.

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:59.960
I suppose running a business
isn't all that straightforward...

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:01.630
Good work there.

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:05.250
U-um, is there anything I can do to help out?

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:07.130
Thanks, Lorea.

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:09.170
Just hearing you say that is plenty.

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:10.170
But...

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:14.210
Oh yeah, you've been sending letters
back and forth with Ms. Leonora, right?

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:17.130
Yeah. I've been asking for Mr. Darna's help.

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:23.000
Then what about asking my dad
to head to South Straug more frequently?

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.790
It would be helpful if you could
keep in frequent contact, right?

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:28.670
Well you see...

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:31.880
I've made something quite nice
to deal with that very issue.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:34.750
Something nice...?

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:47.830
Starting today, I can see a small star

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:51.250
Shining bright in my heart

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:54.540
Whether crying, laughing, or shining

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:56.750
I'll roll up my sleeves and get walking

00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:59.960
(It'll definitely be alright, give your worries the go sign)

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:02.210
(Let's do this right)

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:09.580
Being free can feel so restricting

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:12.920
After all, it never ends

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:16.330
This spiral of theoretical values and test results

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:18.420
Whether I win or lose

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:20.000
(No matter what I try)

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.670
I work hard to see my dream come true

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:23.500
(It's not a cheat, it's a life hack)

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:27.000
I've got the license to take my proper first step

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.250
This is just the beginning

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:33.500
Starting today, I can see a small star

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:36.880
Shining bright in my heart

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:40.250
Whether crying, laughing, or shining

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:42.830
I take a deep breath before work

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:47.000
Resound, as I reach out towards a whole new world

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:50.330
My dream is surely in my hands

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:53.750
An original only I can make

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:56.460
Open that door and say welcome

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:58.960
(This is the start)

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:02.460
(It'll definitely be alright, give your worries the go sign)

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:04.880
(Let's do this right)

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:10.000
What is it, Ms. Sarasa...?

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:13.170
It's an artifact known as a shared sound box.

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:15.380
How do you use it...?

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:19.710
You pour your magical power into it like so...

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:23.080
Testing, testing.

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:25.830
Can you hear me, Ms. Leonora?

00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:28.500
Yes, I sure can!

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:31.880
It's a great success.

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:34.250
Feel free to contact me
whenever you need to.

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:36.080
Right, thank you.

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:37.420
Goodbye.

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:41.630
You can talk with someone
located far away?

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:43.080
That's amazing!

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:47.420
Yeah! What about selling this
shared sound box in the store?

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:51.330
Hmm, that could prove a bit difficult.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:54.500
The standard price for one
would be 500,000 rhea.

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:55.920
500,000?!

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:00.790
Watch out!

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:04.080
M-Ms. Iris?!

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.790
Thank you, Ms. Iris!

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:13.960
I almost lost 500,000 rhea!

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:16.670
Ha, this much is child's play!

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:20.460
If only you had such a smooth catch
back then too...

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:31.130
A-at any rate, not only are
shared sound boxes expensive,

00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:34.330
but most people can't use them without
preparing magical crystals in advance.

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:36.250
And even for people with
a fair bit of magical power,

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:39.500
it can be difficult to reach
beyond the neighboring town...

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:42.830
In other words, it costs a lot to use too.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:46.380
So it really would be best to have
something like the cooling hats

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:49.960
that you could easily use every day, huh?

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:51.750
This is tough...

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:53.170
By the way, Ms. Owner,

00:04:53.170 --> 00:04:56.500
do you have any recommendations
for which ingredients we should gather?

00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:58.170
Ingredients, is it?

00:04:58.170 --> 00:05:01.500
Is there anything we should go after
in place of the frostfang bat fangs?

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:03.540
It would be best if we could
both help you out

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:06.380
and also serve to repay our debt.

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:08.880
Well, let's see...

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:12.250
There are of course
things out there in the forest

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:15.040
that you could gather to
pay off your debt all at once.

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:16.170
That's what we want!

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:17.630
That sounds perfect!

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:19.580
But ingredients like that

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:23.710
would all involve monsters on the
level of the ligarex or greater.

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:25.920
That's...

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:29.080
That's why I think something like
flame stones would be best.

00:05:29.290 --> 00:05:30.580
Flame stones?

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:33.330
The demand for them will go up
with the coming winter,

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:35.420
and the purchase price will rise as well.

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:41.170
But they only come from hellflame
grizzly territory around here.

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:44.290
That sounds dangerous...

00:05:44.290 --> 00:05:45.210
Yeah.

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:49.670
And we still don't know why they
went into a frenzy before either.

00:05:49.670 --> 00:05:51.130
That's true.

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:54.000
Ms. Elyn seemed concerned about that too.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:56.170
In that case, what else...

00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:58.750
What about fruitrot bee honey?

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:01.670
Fruitrot bees...?
Ah, I've heard of them!

00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:03.630
That's a high-class ingredient, isn't it?

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:04.460
Yes.

00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:08.790
Just like their name implies,
fruitrot bees primarily eat rotten fruit.

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:16.170
They tend to go after the fruits stored by
frostfang bats that have spoiled.

00:06:16.670 --> 00:06:19.210
So you should be able to find
a fruitrot bee hive

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:20.670
somewhere near the northern caves.

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:25.210
It's valued highly as raw materials
for high-class honey,

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:29.380
and so the purchase price
greatly exceeds that of regular honey.

00:06:29.710 --> 00:06:32.290
But isn't it dangerous?

00:06:32.290 --> 00:06:33.380
Yes, indeed.

00:06:33.380 --> 00:06:35.040
Of course there's risk.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:38.830
If just anyone could gather it,
it wouldn't go for such a high price.

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:40.210
Of course...

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:41.250
However...

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:45.710
I believe you should be just fine
with insect repellent veils.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:49.750
And you'll also need antidotes for
the off chance that you're stung.

00:06:50.210 --> 00:06:52.250
After all, if things go poorly, you could die!

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:55.040
Die, die, die...

00:06:57.830 --> 00:06:59.000
What should we do...?

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:01.920
I'm somewhat uneasy, but if we
invite Andre's group to assist us,

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:04.000
it should work out...

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:05.040
Yeah.

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:08.250
Alright, we shall follow
your suggestion, Ms. Owner!

00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:14.330
Well then, we're off.

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:16.170
Look forward to our return!

00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:18.040
Take care!

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:22.000
Now then, let's get to work on
the core business at hand.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:22.960
Core business?

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:24.000
Yeah.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:27.170
The most important thing for
expanding the shop's sales

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:30.290
is improving my skills as an alchemist.

00:07:30.290 --> 00:07:31.960
And so...

00:07:33.130 --> 00:07:35.710
I've got to advance further in my
complete alchemy works!

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:40.630
According to my master it gets difficult
around here, so I've got to give my all.

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:43.500
You really are amazing, Ms. Sarasa...

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:45.670
In that case, I should try my hardest too!

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:49.420
I'll take on some dishes
I still haven't tried to make!

00:07:49.420 --> 00:07:51.330
Let's both give it all we've got!

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:52.380
Yeah!

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:53.670
Now then...

00:07:54.290 --> 00:07:57.540
Why don't I try making a
floating tent for today?

00:07:59.170 --> 00:08:01.540
To start, I need to cut the leather...

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:08.420
Is there any sort of artifact out there
to make stitching leather together easier?

00:08:09.790 --> 00:08:13.880
Now it's time to really show my skills!

00:08:27.630 --> 00:08:30.130
Just a little more... A little more...

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:43.380
There they are!

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:48.250
That's a crazy amount!

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:52.330
Alright, let's follow them!

00:08:58.250 --> 00:08:59.750
Come back here!

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:06.080
Did we lose them...?

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:08.380
They certainly are quick little buggers!

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:11.460
Wouldn't we better off just
starting over again at this point?

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:12.380
Yeah.

00:09:12.380 --> 00:09:14.750
No, I'm not giving up!

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:16.250
It's dangerous going on your own.

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:18.040
I'm fine! Don't wo-

00:09:23.170 --> 00:09:24.210
Geez...

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:25.830
I told you so.

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:28.250
Oww...

00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:29.830
I'm terribly ashamed...

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:36.420
What is it, Iri-

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:37.250
Shh!

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:52.710
Around here looks good.

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:58.420
What are you making, Ms. Sarasa?

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:02.250
It's floating!

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:06.790
Huh? A tent?

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:09.580
Yup. It doesn't need
any poles to support it,

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:11.710
and is easy to carry too.

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:14.500
There! All done!

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:16.080
Wow! How convenient!

00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:18.210
Do you want to go inside, Lorea?

00:10:18.210 --> 00:10:20.000
Huh? Can I?

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:21.130
Of course!

00:10:21.130 --> 00:10:22.330
Excuse me, then!

00:10:23.380 --> 00:10:25.330
It's so nice and fluffy!

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:27.580
And it's nice and cool too! This is the best!

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:29.830
I also added the functionality of
the environmental tuning fabric,

00:10:29.830 --> 00:10:31.380
and the capability to repel insects too.

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:34.330
Ms. Sarasa, how much would this cost?

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:37.540
Probably over 100,000 rhea.

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:39.500
So even though I went and made it,

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:42.210
it would probably be a bit difficult
to sell here in the village.

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:45.290
No, it may actually sell just fine!

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:48.000
As I've served our customers,

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:50.040
I've noticed that most gatherers

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:54.040
don't seem to know much about
which sort of artifacts are out there.

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:57.630
Right, it's true that Ms. Iris and
Ms. Kate don't seem to know

00:10:57.630 --> 00:10:59.630
anything about that at all.

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:04.790
So if we display it in front of the shop
and show how convenient it is,

00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:07.080
we might get some interested buyers,
don't you think?

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:08.580
I see...!

00:11:09.290 --> 00:11:10.500
Lorea...

00:11:10.790 --> 00:11:14.420
You've been thinking that seriously
about the shop?

00:11:14.630 --> 00:11:16.040
What do you think...?

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:19.420
Do you think we could talk
a bit more about that idea?

00:11:19.420 --> 00:11:23.170
While eating your cooking, perhaps?

00:11:23.170 --> 00:11:24.420
Of course!

00:11:27.130 --> 00:11:28.330
Welcome back.

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:30.040
We were just about to eat-

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:32.750
I'm borrowing the toilet, Ms. Owner!

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:34.880
We're back!

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:36.380
Welcome back.

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:38.580
Were you able to gather the honey?

00:11:38.580 --> 00:11:39.460
Indeed.

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:41.880
Just look!

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:43.830
Wow, you got so much!

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:46.710
Even so, it's only half of
what we gathered in total.

00:11:46.710 --> 00:11:48.790
I can buy it all off of you, right?

00:11:48.790 --> 00:11:50.500
Yes, please do.

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:51.630
Right!

00:11:51.830 --> 00:11:54.750
Just hold on.
I'm running the calculations.

00:11:54.750 --> 00:11:56.790
What happened with Mr. Andre's group?

00:11:56.790 --> 00:12:00.330
They headed back to the inn.
Their stomachs were feeling a bit off.

00:12:00.330 --> 00:12:01.790
Just like Ms. Kate?

00:12:01.790 --> 00:12:05.750
Indeed. Perhaps the food
we brought along had gone bad.

00:12:05.960 --> 00:12:07.790
Oh, is that so?

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:09.830
Though it's autumn now
it's still hot out,

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:11.960
so you have to be careful with food...

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:15.380
Wait, just to be certain...

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:19.000
Mr. Andre and everyone didn't taste
any fruitrot bee honey, did they?

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:21.000
Well, we had just a bit.

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:22.420
You ate it?!

00:12:23.540 --> 00:12:25.960
I-it really was presumptuous to eat

00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:29.170
such a high quality food while
being indebted, wasn't it...?

00:12:29.170 --> 00:12:31.920
But the temptation of the honey
just won out...

00:12:31.920 --> 00:12:32.960
You dummy!

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:35.460
Don't be stupid!
That doesn't matter at all!

00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:36.080
Huh?

00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:39.420
You can't just eat
fruitrot bee honey as is!

00:12:39.420 --> 00:12:40.750
It's poisonous!

00:12:40.750 --> 00:12:41.710
Huh?!

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:57.290
P-poisonous?!

00:12:57.420 --> 00:13:00.040
B-but it's high-class honey...

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:02.170
It's the base ingredient for that!

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:04.920
They're bees that eat rotten fruits!

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:08.040
I recommended it because
other animals and monsters

00:13:08.040 --> 00:13:10.380
don't go after them thanks to the poison!

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:14.750
Agh! Who ate how much?!

00:13:14.750 --> 00:13:17.880
I-I think everyone had a spoonful,

00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:20.420
though Andre's group may have
eaten a little more...

00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:24.130
That much won't be enough to kill you.

00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:25.790
Thank goodness...!

00:13:25.790 --> 00:13:26.920
However...

00:13:26.920 --> 00:13:28.290
For the time being,

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:31.670
you'll be forming a contract of
close partnership with the toilet.

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:33.750
A contract of partner...?

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:40.750
P-please excuse me for a moment!

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:46.040
Kate! H-hurry up and get out of there!

00:13:46.040 --> 00:13:47.710
No can do. This door won't
be opening for a while.

00:13:47.710 --> 00:13:50.210
Don't say that! I'm begging you!
Just for a little!

00:13:50.210 --> 00:13:51.830
Sorry. Just wait for a bit longer.

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:53.580
I can't wait! I'm at my limit!

00:13:53.580 --> 00:13:54.830
I just can't. Ow...!

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:56.880
Even when I'm begging you so?!

00:13:56.880 --> 00:14:00.960
Iris, when we headed out didn't you say
that we were equal allies?

00:14:01.290 --> 00:14:03.790
If we're even, then please,
give my dignity priority here...

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:07.080
H-half, then! Just half would be fine!

00:14:07.080 --> 00:14:08.290
Let's share!

00:14:08.290 --> 00:14:09.670
Are we not best friends?

00:14:10.170 --> 00:14:12.710
This is one thing that even
best friends can't share!

00:14:15.920 --> 00:14:18.290
Ms. Owner...? A hoe...?

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:25.630
Ms. Iris...

00:14:26.540 --> 00:14:29.710
This is all that I can do for you now.

00:14:29.960 --> 00:14:32.960
No one should be able to see you
behind the tent...

00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:40.790
Kate! I won't be forgetting this humiliation!

00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:46.960
Now then, Lorea, we've faced
a bit of a disaster...

00:14:46.960 --> 00:14:49.330
Yes, it truly was a tragedy.

00:14:49.330 --> 00:14:53.330
I should have explained better
about the rotfruit bee honey...

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:55.880
It's not your fault, Ms. Sarasa!

00:14:55.880 --> 00:14:59.500
I never imagined they wouldn't have
known it was poisonous...

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:01.330
Is there medicine for it?

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:04.000
There is, however...

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:08.170
While this will work on all sorts
of poisons, it's expensive.

00:15:08.540 --> 00:15:10.880
Though they went and got all that honey,

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:13.210
if things go poorly,
they could still end up in the red.

00:15:14.630 --> 00:15:17.920
But fortunately, there are hardly
any cases out there of people dying

00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:19.920
from the poison in fruitrot bee honey.

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:23.630
Alright, how about we try making a
specialized antidote as soon as possible?

00:15:23.630 --> 00:15:25.380
Will you lend me a hand, Lorea?

00:15:25.380 --> 00:15:26.290
Of course!

00:15:26.290 --> 00:15:28.290
I'll do anything I can to help!

00:15:30.210 --> 00:15:32.290
Are you alright, Ms. Iris?

00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:34.460
Just take it easy here.

00:15:34.460 --> 00:15:36.790
There's water and a blanket there for you.

00:15:37.130 --> 00:15:40.420
Please, take care of Kate too...

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:42.040
Of course!

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:44.130
I'll have medicine made up for you soon.

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:45.580
Let's get going, Lorea.

00:15:45.580 --> 00:15:46.500
Right!

00:15:48.580 --> 00:15:51.830
It's fairly simple to get ahold of
the ingredients themselves.

00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:53.670
Ah, there's one!

00:15:54.290 --> 00:15:55.330
Perfect.

00:15:55.710 --> 00:15:57.670
Could you look for
more bugs like this one?

00:15:57.670 --> 00:15:58.790
Got it.

00:15:59.290 --> 00:16:01.500
How many do you need?

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:04.130
Well, it's about ten for each person,

00:16:04.130 --> 00:16:07.790
so to allow a little extra,
let's say around 60?

00:16:07.790 --> 00:16:10.040
And this will make for a medicine?

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:12.500
Right. The ingredients are cheap
in and of themselves,

00:16:12.500 --> 00:16:14.210
but it takes some effort to prepare.

00:16:14.210 --> 00:16:15.630
But we have to hurry.

00:16:15.630 --> 00:16:17.920
So we'll omit some steps this time.

00:16:17.920 --> 00:16:19.170
You're skipping steps?

00:16:19.460 --> 00:16:21.670
It's not like it'll make it less effective.

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:28.710
Hang in there, Ms. Kate!

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:30.750
Just hold on a little longer!

00:16:39.460 --> 00:16:41.210
Is that good?

00:16:41.210 --> 00:16:42.290
Yeah.

00:16:42.710 --> 00:16:45.790
There's no time to dissect them one by one...

00:16:48.170 --> 00:16:50.380
So we'll go ahead and
crush them down like so.

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:54.080
You're supposed to drink
this medicine, right?

00:16:54.630 --> 00:16:56.080
Want to give it a taste test?

00:16:56.630 --> 00:16:58.290
Oh, no thank you!

00:16:58.290 --> 00:16:59.580
No surprise there.

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:04.250
Well by adding water and stirring a bit
while adding magical power,

00:17:04.250 --> 00:17:06.000
it may improve at least a little.

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:07.830
A little, you say...?

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:10.750
Yeah, just a bit,
but it's the thought that counts.

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:16.380
The waves have finally abated...

00:17:16.920 --> 00:17:18.330
Sorry for the wait!

00:17:18.330 --> 00:17:20.130
Your medicine is ready!

00:17:20.330 --> 00:17:23.040
This potion will heal you right up!

00:17:24.500 --> 00:17:28.380
But it would cause your debt to grow,
and dramatically at that.

00:17:29.380 --> 00:17:30.880
And so...

00:17:31.790 --> 00:17:34.670
I made a cheap version
where that won't be a problem.

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:38.580
It's a bit less effective,
but with your resiliences

00:17:38.580 --> 00:17:40.750
it shouldn't be an issue,
so that's no worry.

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:43.580
I am truly grateful...!

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:46.210
Go ahead, drink up.

00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:52.080
Please, gulp it down!

00:17:52.080 --> 00:17:55.250
Don't think anything or even look,
just chug it down in a single go!

00:17:55.250 --> 00:17:56.750
What is this stuff?!

00:17:56.750 --> 00:17:59.000
I-it'll work, won't it?

00:17:59.210 --> 00:18:02.290
Of course! I wouldn't give you
something that wouldn't help.

00:18:02.290 --> 00:18:03.500
But...

00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:05.750
Feel free to go first, Kate.

00:18:05.750 --> 00:18:07.460
Oh no, go right ahead, Iris.

00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:08.960
Ah, no, you first.

00:18:08.960 --> 00:18:10.130
No, you.

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:13.500
If you dawdle too long,
the next wave will come.

00:18:14.380 --> 00:18:18.670
Who will be the one to head into
the backyard this time around...?

00:18:18.880 --> 00:18:20.630
I-I'll drink it first!

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:24.830
S-she drank it...!

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:33.750
Here.

00:18:38.170 --> 00:18:40.330
Are you alright?

00:18:40.330 --> 00:18:42.750
S-somehow...

00:18:43.380 --> 00:18:46.290
It's your turn next, Ms. Kate.

00:18:51.880 --> 00:18:54.420
What's wrong?
Hurry up and drink it too, Kate.

00:18:54.420 --> 00:18:58.580
Y-you'll need someone to look after you
until you're better, right, Iris?

00:18:58.580 --> 00:19:01.750
So I'll go ahead and drink this potion...

00:19:02.290 --> 00:19:04.330
Give up.

00:19:04.330 --> 00:19:06.080
B-but...

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:10.210
Stop complaining and drink it!

00:19:10.210 --> 00:19:13.130
We mustn't let the owner's kindness
go to waste, right?

00:19:13.130 --> 00:19:15.500
H-hold on! Let me prepare myself!

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:17.290
Resign yourself!

00:19:32.920 --> 00:19:34.080
Oh, what is it?

00:19:34.080 --> 00:19:36.380
You want water? This water, perhaps?

00:19:36.380 --> 00:19:37.830
So greedy!

00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:47.670
You're holding a grudge over that
thing with the toilet, aren't you?

00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:50.830
Whatever do you mean?

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:53.880
The next wave... Excuse me!

00:19:54.330 --> 00:19:55.670
Ah, hold on...!

00:19:58.580 --> 00:20:00.380
Are they going to be okay?

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:02.960
Yeah. The medicine should take effect

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:04.960
in less than an hour and
make them feel better.

00:20:04.960 --> 00:20:06.630
It's my turn now!

00:20:06.630 --> 00:20:07.830
No, me!

00:20:13.460 --> 00:20:15.750
Seriously, thanks.

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:20.040
Who knows what would have become of us
by now without your medicine.

00:20:20.040 --> 00:20:22.210
That taste was unbelievably bad, though.

00:20:22.210 --> 00:20:25.040
I'm just glad to see you all feeling better!

00:20:25.630 --> 00:20:28.000
By the way, this thing is amazing.

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:30.170
It sure seems convenient!

00:20:30.330 --> 00:20:32.750
And this one doesn't seem to be a tent...

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:35.170
It's a toilet?

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:37.540
It's prefabricated.

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:39.210
Lorea had the idea,

00:20:39.210 --> 00:20:42.460
and so I'm going ahead and
displaying the artifacts I made.

00:20:42.750 --> 00:20:45.710
You never know where demand
will come from, after all.

00:20:45.710 --> 00:20:47.500
Ooh, how interesting.

00:20:47.500 --> 00:20:50.210
It could definitely be helpful
when out camping.

00:20:51.040 --> 00:20:54.750
I see. I never knew
stuff like this even existed!

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:58.040
Alright, I'll take it!
How much does it cost?

00:21:00.920 --> 00:21:03.000
That certainly was a surprise.

00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:06.960
I never expected Mr. Andrea's group
to buy a floating tent!

00:21:06.960 --> 00:21:08.500
Thanks, Lorea!

00:21:08.500 --> 00:21:09.670
Oh, no.

00:21:09.670 --> 00:21:14.750
Thanks to you, the gatherers have
had more money to spend too.

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:17.880
And the quality of your products
is always guaranteed!

00:21:17.880 --> 00:21:20.710
Yes, that tent was truly splendid!

00:21:21.210 --> 00:21:23.460
If only the prefabricated toilet
was ready too,

00:21:23.460 --> 00:21:25.080
then it would have been perfect...

00:21:26.040 --> 00:21:27.130
That's certainly true.

00:21:27.130 --> 00:21:31.500
Still, I'm glad to see that the
two of you have fully recovered.

00:21:31.500 --> 00:21:35.130
Yeah. I'm sorry we're always
causing you such trouble.

00:21:35.130 --> 00:21:36.580
My deepest apologies.

00:21:36.580 --> 00:21:38.500
We'll take better care in the future.

00:21:38.500 --> 00:21:40.920
We have to help one another out
when we're in need.

00:21:42.380 --> 00:21:44.000
Ah, welcome!

00:21:52.420 --> 00:21:53.630
Father?!

00:21:53.920 --> 00:21:55.040
Mama?!

00:21:56.460 --> 00:21:57.670
But why...?!

00:22:01.080 --> 00:22:04.960
Ms. Iris's father and
Ms. Kate's mother...?!

00:22:24.500 --> 00:22:30.210
The sunlight gently streams in through my window

00:22:30.500 --> 00:22:36.000
Whispering that it's time to get up

00:22:36.420 --> 00:22:42.040
Bringing my anticipation and a bit of courage with me

00:22:42.420 --> 00:22:47.580
I set off to look for a tiny bit of growth

00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:53.920
Peering lightly through the door opened for the first time

00:22:53.920 --> 00:23:01.460
My heart is pounding, alongside plenty of smiles

00:23:02.130 --> 00:23:09.040
Squeezing in plenty of new encounters

00:23:09.040 --> 00:23:14.250
Each time we mingle, a harmony is born

00:23:14.420 --> 00:23:21.290
I want to believe in every possibility

00:23:21.290 --> 00:23:29.330
Just like I believe this sky will be clear again tomorrow

